kers can do  in this regard is to obviously stop  smoking altogether  now i know for most of the smokers it  can be an impossible task  but you can always try there are plenty  of resources available on the internet  for smoking the addiction  and i will leave all the relevant links  in the description bar down below  nevertheless if you're not planning on  quitting anytime soon  what you can do is reduce your frequency  of smoking  that is very important for non-smokers  it is also very important to avoid  secondhand smoke  while quitting smoking is the most  important thing you can do for your  lungs  it's crucial not to breathe in other  people's smoke as well  use face masks in places where there is  high level of air pollution  the air passages in our lungs have  microscopic finger like projections on  them  known as celia the celia and sticky  mucus  work together to protect the lungs from  infection  the mucus traps any bacteria or  pathogens as they enter the lungs  and the celia move in a synchronized  pattern to move the mucus  up into the airway back into our throat  where it can be swallowed  and any pathogens can be killed by the  acidity of the stomach  if we are smoking constantly or we are  getting exposed to high levels of air  pollution  the cilia in our lungs do not function  properly and they are unable to clear  our lungs from various particles in the  smoke  as well as bacteria and other pathogens  so if you want to detoxify our lungs and  implement the other methods  we are going to talk about next in this  video it is very important first that we  reduce our exposure to smoke  and other forms of pollution this allows  our celia to function properly  and help in the recovery of lungs in a  much better way  number second thing to do is to control  your indoor air pollution  indoor air quality also contributes to  lung diseases  dust irritants and chemicals can build  up in your home  people with lung diseases usually spend  a lot of time indoors  and it's important to do so on days when  outdoor air quality is poor  here are few suggestions to help improve  the indoor air quality  clean up vacuum oftenly and invest in a  good quality vacuum cleaner  mop your floors but try not to use  chemical laden cleaners  dehumidify your rooms dust and mold  grow very quickly in a humid environment  use a dehumidifier or keep your exhaust  fan running while cooking  to prevent the growth of mould test for  radon gas  radon is a radioactive gas occurring  naturally in the ground  and it contributes to lung cancer it can  get in your home from the foundation  pick up a radon test kit at any home  improvement store  go chemical free use natural cleaning  products  fragrance free products and avoid  aerosol sprays  purify the air inside your home indoor  plants such as  fern spider or aloe vera can help purify  air you can also use an air purifier  i have included links to some of the  best air purifiers that automatically  sense the air quality  and remove 99.97 airborne pollutants  as small as 0.003 microns  so these were the first two things in  our list cutting down or completely  avoiding smoking  and avoiding outdoor air pollution and  cutting down the levels of indoor air  pollution  now let's talk about the ways you can  detox your lungs  these include postural drainage proper  diet and exercise  let's talk about them one by one so  number one thing is postural drainage  postural drainage is the drainage of  lung secretions  using gravity in postural drainage the  patient's body is positioned so that the  trachea  is inclined downwards frames tilt tables  and pillows may be used to support  patients in these positions  here are some techniques to perform  personal drainage  number one position is done by lying on  your back  lie down on the floor or a bed place  pillows under the hips to ensure that  the chest is lower than the hips  then slowly inhale through your nose and  exhale through your mouth  each exhale 