ype of exercises you can do  for better lung health are breathing  exercises  breathing exercises help to improve the  lung function and lung capacity as well  especially for individuals who are  smokers who have smoked in the past  or who have lung damage from a chronic  lung disease now there are many types of  breathing exercises  for example diaphragmatic breathing  burst lip breathing etc  i will leave links to some of these  videos in the description box down below  that will explain the procedure of how  you perform these exercises  so this was about the exercises you  should do to help to recover your lungs  to a healthy state  now let's talk about some of the things  you should include in your diet for lung  detox  number one is green tea green tea  contains many antioxidants that help to  reduce  inflammation in the lungs these  compounds may even protect the lung  tissue from the harmful effects of smoke  inhalation  a recent study involving more than one  thousand adults in korea  reported that people who drank at least  two cups of green tea per day  had better lung function than those who  drank none  you can also include vitamin d in your  diet a vitamin d  rich diet also improves your lung health  the best  food sources of vitamin d are usually  animal products such as salmon  sardines eggs milk butter etc  make sure to give 10 to 20 minutes of  exposure to sunlight per day  so that the vitamin in your body could  be converted into its active form  you should also include antioxidant  foods in your diet  nutrient dense foods especially those  abundant in antioxidants are well known  for helping the lungs  recover to their optimal health  antioxidant rich diet helps to  neutralize the free radicals  that damage the lung cells thus it is  very important to consume foods that are  packed with antioxidants to promote  overall lung health  some of these foods include apples which  contain a variety of phytochemicals  including quercetin catechin fluorescein  and chlorogenic acid  all of which are strong antioxidants red  bell peppers also contain  abundant antioxidants vitamin c and  carotenoids  turmeric and its powerful ingredient  curcumin have powerful antioxidant  health benefits  as well blueberries are believed to have  one of the highest antioxidant levels  of all common fruits and vegetables the  main antioxidant compounds in  blueberries are known as  flavonoids some other very good foods  that have  abundant antioxidants include green  leafy vegetables  lentils beans grapes walnuts and garlic  so these were some of the foods that you  should include in your diet  that will help in your lung detox  process you can also consider taking  antioxidant supplementation  i have included links to some of the  best antioxidants i have found in the  description box down below  i hope you liked the video if you did  support us by hitting the like button  below  and you can also support med simplified  by clicking the join button below or  joining us  on patreon page all links are in the  description box down below  thank you so much for watching this  video see you in the next one

